  },
  "question_text": "<p>If an SPI sensor datasheet states &quot;data is sampled on the rising edge, and the clock idles high,&quot; what are the correct CPOL and CPHA settings?</p>",
  "answer_text": "<p>CPOL = 1, CPHA = 1.</p>",
  "explanation_text": "<p>CPOL=1 means the clock idles high. Because it idles high, the first edge is falling. CPHA=1 means data is sampled on the second edge (the rising edge).</p>\n<img src=\"{{image_1}}\" alt=\"A timing diagram showing a single SPI clock cycle starting HIGH (idle), falling (first edge), then rising (second edge). A dashed line on the rising edge says &quot;Sample Data.&quot;\" style=\"max-width:100%;margin:1rem 0;border-radius:6px;\"/>",
  "bonus_question_text": "<p>If CPHA was set to 0, when would data be sampled?</p>",
  "bonus_answer_text": "<p>Data would be sampled on the first edge (the falling edge).</p>",
